In Britain, a "palais" refers to a public hall or venue for dancing.

TIP:  The Kinks play the outro using (D#) and (Bb).  (D#) is (D) up one fret with the pinky covering the 4th string/5th fret (striking only the bottom 4 strings).  (Bb) can be played as usual or as an (F) form on the 6th fret.  And since you're already playing (D#) in the 3rd fret it's really which is more comfortable for you to play.  And if you don't care whether you're matching the original recording I've found it easier to take it up a full step and play (E) and (A) instead.  Both chord strings are presented as the outro.


